<p>This policy explains what we collect about the people who use Shadetree, why, and the choices you have. For the data businesses keep about their own clients in Shadetree, see the <%= link_to "Data Processing Summary", legal_document_path("data-processing") %>: there, the business decides and we process it for them.</p>

<h2>What we collect</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Your account:</strong> your name, email, a hashed password, and the businesses and roles you have.</li>
  <li><strong>Your business:</strong> what you enter (name, contact details, logo, settings) and what you create (clients, quotes, jobs, invoices).</li>
  <li><strong>Sign-in and security:</strong> the browsers you're signed in on, IP addresses and times, so you can see your sessions and we can stop abuse.</li>
  <li><strong>Billing:</strong> your plan and payment history. Card details are handled by our payment provider; we don't see or store them.</li>
  <li><strong>Usage:</strong> visits to our public website, counted without cookies or personal identifiers by analytics we run ourselves.</li>
  <li><strong>Messages:</strong> what you send us when you contact us.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Why we use it</h2>
<ul>
  <li>To provide Shadetree: signing you in, saving your work, sending the emails you ask us to send.</li>
  <li>To keep it secure and stop spam and abuse.</li>
  <li>To bill you for a paid plan.</li>
  <li>To answer you, and to tell you about changes that affect your account. We don't send marketing emails unless you ask for them.</li>
</ul>
<p>We don't sell personal data, and we don't use it for advertising.</p>

<h2>Cookies</h2>
<p>We only use cookies that Shadetree needs to work: keeping you signed in, remembering this browser, and protecting forms. We don't use advertising or tracking cookies, so there's no cookie banner.</p>

<h2>Who else handles it</h2>
<p>A few companies help us run Shadetree, such as our hosting, email delivery and payment providers. They're listed on our <%= link_to "Sub-processors", legal_document_path("subprocessors") %> page and may only use the data to provide their service to us.</p>

<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Account and business data: while your account is open. When you delete your account, your personal details are removed straight away; records a business keeps (like invoices you created) stay with that business, without your name.</li>
  <li>Sign-in records: up to 90 days.</li>
  <li>Backups: up to 30 days, then overwritten.</li>
  <li>Billing records: as long as tax law requires.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
<p>You can see and change your details on your account page, download your business's data, and delete your account at any time. Depending on where you live, you may also have the right to ask what we hold about you, to correct it, to object to how we use it, or to complain to a data protection authority. Contact us and we'll respond within 30 days.</p>

<h2>Security</h2>
<p>See <%= link_to "Security & Trust", legal_document_path("security") %> for how we protect your data.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Shadetree, [registered company name and address, to be confirmed]. Privacy questions: <%= link_to "contact us", contact_path %>.</p>
